homelab-dns (0.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Warm the Lua health-check state at every start (post-cutover #107):
    /usr/lib/homelab-dns/homelab-dns-warm-lua, run as ExecStartPost by the
    pdns.service drop-in homelab-warm-lua.conf, lists every LUA record
    (pdnsutil), queries each once at the local address so PowerDNS starts
    checking its addresses, waits one check round and logs what is answered
    now. Without it a fresh PowerDNS hands the first client of every record
    all of the record's addresses, dead edges included (seen at the pve2
    reboot of 2026-11-27). Never fails the unit. Depends on libnet-dns-perl.
    t/warm-lua.t runs at build time. Takes effect at the next pdns start.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:30:00 -0600

